 "chunks": [
  {
   "text": "In 1969, Sergei Stepanov found an elementary way to prove such bounds.",
   "start": 0.75,
   "end": 6.15
  },
  {
   "text": "Its engine is simple.",
   "start": 6.15,
   "end": 7.987
  },
  {
   "text": "A polynomial of degree D has at most D roots, counted with multiplicity:",
   "start": 7.987,
   "end": 12.737
  },
  {
   "text": "a double root counts twice.",
   "start": 12.737,
   "end": 14.725
  },
  {
   "text": "So build an auxiliary polynomial, not identically zero,",
   "start": 15.65,
   "end": 19.375
  },
  {
   "text": "which is the hard part, that vanishes at every one of the N solutions,",
   "start": 19.375,
   "end": 23.4
  },
  {
   "text": "each to order m.",
   "start": 23.4,
   "end": 24.325
  },
  {
   "text": "Counting roots gives N times m, at most D.",
   "start": 24.325,
   "end": 27.175
  },
  {
   "text": "Raising m spreads a fixed overhead thinner, about p over m,",
   "start": 27.175,
   "end": 31.225
  },
  {
   "text": "but every extra order of vanishing costs extra degree,",
   "start": 31.225,
   "end": 34.788
  },
  {
   "text": "about m.",
   "start": 34.788,
   "end": 35.525
  },
  {
   "text": "The two balance when m is about root p.",
   "start": 35.525,
   "end": 37.725
  },
  {
   "text": "Multiplicity of about root p yields an error of about root p.",
   "start": 37.725,
   "end": 41.2
  }
 ],
